{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/509875-a-few-questions-i-hope-someone-can-help-with","id":509875,"title":"A few questions I hope someone can help with.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-10T08:53:04-07:00","id":509875,"title":"A few questions I hope someone can help with.","content":"I've recently acquired all the core books for the series and have been going through them and taking notes for some ideas for a campaign.<br /> So I was hoping someone here could help me with a few things I was wondering about?<br /> <br /> In the core book it mentions Jack Cross (pg 321) and I figured he'd probably be of &quot;The Pure&quot; group The Predator Kings. I don't know for sure if that fits with his description in the book (which can be changed of course) but was wondering if that was close? Does the The Forsaken Core or another Forsaken books explain how the wolves of both sides hunt in a city and what they hunt and how often?<br /> <br /> I also got a copy of the starter demos and in one, which I'd like to use, it refers to an artifact used by the founding fathers to gain control over the colonies and lead the revolt. It was founded by Thomas Jefferson and described as piece of limestone with an unknown fossil protruding from its surface. Does anyone have an idea what it could be? I was thinking it might be a Dendera Relief (Reliquary, Pg 57).<br /> <br /> Though I know this one if from VTR: Mythologies, I consider it a hunter still. There's a reference on Pg 137 of The Hunter a creature that took out a night club in Philadelphia. I was hoping to use it for the Hunters to encounter again. I know it's a Blade knock off but was wondering if anyone can think of a creature in any of the books that might come close to what was describe?<br /> <br /> Thanks for taking the time to answer my post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T10:08:13-07:00","id":509975,"title":"","content":"The pure don't generally hunt in the cities, they're not urban werewolves, that's the forsaken, the predator kings especially. It's a sin for a predator king to use a cell phone, wear man made clothes, or ride in a car. When they do hunt, they hunt forsaken for the war, humans for food.<br /> <br /> Jefferson's limestone doesn't sound at all like a dendera relief.<br /> <br /> The hunter is specifically an artificial life form, so promethean or imbued, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:26:14-07:00","id":510180,"title":"","content":"Thanks for replying.<br /> <br /> I don't have the book for the Forsaken so what I found online I would guess perhaps either Cross is a Blood Talon or is not a part of the Moon Tribes at all which would be fine with me. I suppose there could be Packs of Wolves with no actual tribes.<br /> <br /> As for the Relic I will change it up. See what I can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:38:01-07:00","id":510202,"title":"","content":"He sounds more like an Ivory Claw, if I had to pick a Pure tribe for him. On the Forsaken side of things he'd probably be an Iron Master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}